# Helm Rules

## Chart Structure

Single generic chart shared by all 8 services:

```
helm/petclinic-service/
├── Chart.yaml
├── values.yaml
└── templates/
    ├── _helpers.tpl
    ├── deployment.yaml
    ├── service.yaml
    ├── configmap.yaml
    ├── serviceaccount.yaml
    ├── hpa.yaml
    ├── pdb.yaml
    └── NOTES.txt
```

## Values Hierarchy

ArgoCD merges last-wins:

1. `helm/petclinic-service/values.yaml` — chart defaults
2. `helm-values/{service}.yaml` — ports, env, init containers, image.name
3. `helm-values/{env}.yaml` — replicas, HPA/PDB, `image.registry`

## Per-Service Values

Each service file MUST specify `service.port`, `image.name` (service name only), `springProfiles`, `env`, `secrets`, and `initContainers`.

## Per-Environment Values

- `dev.yaml` — 1 replica, no HPA/PDB, registry `petclinic-dev`
- `prod.yaml` — 2 replicas, HPA/PDB per service, registry `petclinic-prod`

Registry is `{account_id}.dkr.ecr.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/petclinic-{env}`. **Never hardcode an AWS account ID.**

## Templates

- Use `_helpers.tpl` for labels/names/selectors
- Conditional HPA/PDB/ConfigMap with `{{- if .Values.x.enabled }}`
- NEVER put secrets in values files — ExternalSecret CRs in `k8s/base/external-secrets/`
- Default `image.tag` must not be `latest`. Use an empty string or `changeme` that CI overwrites with a SHA

## Validation

```bash
helm template petclinic helm/petclinic-service/ \
  -f helm-values/{service}.yaml \
  -f helm-values/{env}.yaml
helm lint helm/petclinic-service/ \
  -f helm-values/{service}.yaml \
  -f helm-values/{env}.yaml
```

## Startup Order

- config-server: no init containers
- discovery-server: wait for config-server:8888
- all others: wait for config-server and discovery-server
